solution_md:
Hopefully you mean Jeff's investment fell by *** $\frac{m}{n}$ *** where  $m$  and  $n$  are relatively prime positive integers, not:
<blockquote>In June Jeff’s investment fell by where  $m$  and  $n$  are relatively prime positive integers.</blockquote>
<details><summary>Solution</summary>Writing all this as a product of fractions with starting investment  $1$ , we equate this to  $1$  to get:
\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{\cancel{7}}{\cancel{4}}\right)\left(\frac{\cancel{3}}{\cancel{4}}\right)\left(\frac{\cancel{4}}{\cancel{3}}\right)\left(\frac{\cancel{4}}{5}\right)\left(\frac{8}{\cancel{7}}\right)\left(1-\frac{m}{n}\right)&= 1  \frac58&=1-\frac{m}{n}  \frac{m}{n}&=\frac38  m&=3  n&=8  m+n&=\boxed{11}
\end{align*}</details>

