Let  $AE$  intersect  $WXYZ$  again at point  $V$ .  By Menelaus on  $\triangle ABZ$  with transversal  $WXZ$ , compute  $\tfrac{CZ}{ZB} = \tfrac 65\cdot\tfrac 29 = \tfrac 4{15}$ .  Furthermore, observe that, since  $\tfrac{AW}{WB} = \tfrac 29 = \tfrac{EY}{YD}$ , points  $W$  and  $Y$  are symmetric with respect to the midline of parallelogram  $ABED$  pareallel to  $BE$ ; it follows by symmetry that  $WY$  passes through the midpoint of  $\overline{AE}$ , i.e.  $AV = VE$ .  Another application of Menelaus on  $\triangle ABE$  with transversal  $WVZ$  yields  $\tfrac{EZ}{ZB} = \tfrac 29$ .

Without loss of generality, let  $BZ = 45$ .  The above computations imply  $CZ = 12$  and  $EZ = 10$ .  Now observe that  $BC = BZ - BC = 33$ , so  $EF = 33$  and  $FZ = FE - EZ = 23$ .  This means  $\tfrac{EZ}{FZ} = \tfrac{10}{23}$ , and the requested answer is  $\boxed{33}$ .

